WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:03.470
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.570
I'm Go Onizuka.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:11.290
The real hero has arrived to unmask the fake hero!

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.760
Appear, my circuit!

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.460
Link Summon!

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:24.340
Appear, Link 3 Gouki The Great Ogre!

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.800
When Great Ogre is in the Monster Zone...

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.750
...all faceup monsters lose ATK equal to their DEF!

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.480
Take this!  Ogre Pressure!

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.920
Twistcobra's effect activates!

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:50.460
By tributing Riscorpio, Great Ogre gains his ATK until the end of the turn!

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:59.740
Due to Headbatt's effect, Great Ogre gains 800 ATK until the end of the turn!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.760
This is my finisher!

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.700
I run Across the universe

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.870
At the speed of light

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.740
Begin Loading

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.470
Open the door of dreams

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:37.040
VRAINS spreads

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.150
Believe in myself

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.680
VRAINS continues

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:48.990
The circuit draws the future

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:53.060
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.660
Access!

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.360
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:58.970
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.270
Link with my soul

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.040
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.770
Now Win the Race

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.610
Connected world

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:12.110
No matter when

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.480
Nothing is impossible

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.620
Strive for hope

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:24.190
And ride the wind!

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.850
We're in trouble!

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.580
A single blow will end us!

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.220
Stop panicking!

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.050
I activate the trap card, Cyberse Shatter.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.490
It negates the change in your monster's ATK.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.930
And I draw one card.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.970
Huh?  If you used Cyberse Shatter on Twistcobra...

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.900
...you could have prevented more damage.  So why?

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.480
Due to this effect, even if you attack...

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.650
...he'll have 100 LP left.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:21.260
Silence!  100 LP is like a candle in the wind!

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.850
Great Ogre, annihilate Cyberse Wizard!

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.180
Take this!  Ogre Axe!

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.900
I end my turn.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.960
See that!  That's how Charisma Duelist Go Onizuka duels!

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:58.080
Whoa!  Go Onizuka swung his mighty Ogre Axe!

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.540
LINK VRAINS's newest hero - Playmaker - made a misplay!

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.120
He's hanging on by the skin of his teeth!

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.530
I knew Onizuka was better!

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.000
Playmaker is nothing special.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:14.740
It'll be fine now, right?

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.170
Onizuka will win?

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.740
Yes.  Most likely.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:22.760
Did Playmaker really make a misplay?

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.110
He does only have 100 LP left...

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.050
Good.  Defeat Playmaker and acquire the Ignis.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.440
The escape route is finished!

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.760
He can leave through there!

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:45.000
Yusaku!  Stop dueling and leave LINK VRAINS!

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.220
Look!  You can escape through there!

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.500
Log out!  Hurry!

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:10.060
W-Why didn't you go through?

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.530
Since I accepted this duel, I can't flee.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.990
What is Yusaku thinking!

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:21.430
Humans take actions that are impossible to understand.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.900
What are you thinking, Playmaker?

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.780
There are three reasons I'm continuing this duel.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:32.910
#1: He's using various tactics to entertain the crowd.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.980
Even me, his opponent.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.290
Entertain you?

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.850
By putting himself in a pinch?

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.350
That's illogical.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:47.610
No matter when or who he's facing, he'll keep doing his own style.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.260
That's the dueling he believes in.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:55.200
It proves that he's a proud, first-rate duelist.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.670
You seriously think his dueling is first-rate?

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:03.780
#2: He is determined to win this duel.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.250
Entertaining and winning are contradictory.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:11.310
Yes.  But when those contradictions unite...

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:15.220
...you achieve a state of mind that can't be reached rationally.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.460
That is what he's achieved.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:23.160
#3:  Therefore, I now want to duel him to the end.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.630
I'll defeat him with superior dueling!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:29.100
That's my style as a duelist!

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.570
Cannot comprehend!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.040
My turn!

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:37.980
I summon Draconnet from my hand!

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:45.600
Its effect lets me Special Summon a Level 2 or lower Normal Monster...

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.040
... from my hand or deck in defense position.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.610
Appear from my deck, Bitron!

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:57.730
Take this!  Ogre Pressure!

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:04.470
What an annoying effect!

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.940
Actually, everything is now ready.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.910
W-W-What?

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.840
Appear!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.660
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.230
The summoning condition is one Normal Monster.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.340
I set Bitron in the Link Marker!

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.300
Circuit combine!

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:44.800
Link Summon!  Appear, Link 1 Link Spider!

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.150
Link Spider's effect!

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:59.680
From my hand, I Special Summon a Level 4 or lower monster next to this card's link arrow.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.590
Come, Bitron!

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.250
You Link Summoned a weakling?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:11.040
I'll use Ogre Pressure to lower its ATK.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:14.510
Oh my!  Onizuka is correct!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.680
What are you thinking, Playmaker!

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.220
You shouldn't be calm!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.210
I'm saying you're in real trouble!

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:24.650
Stop panicking!

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:31.090
I was waiting for this moment!

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:32.340
What?

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.930
What's he planning to do?

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:41.670
Playmaker plans to activate a Skill that can only be used when he has 1000 or fewer LP.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:46.140
What?  So he took my attacks on purpose to lower his LP?

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.110
Highly likely.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.010
That punk!

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.340
He's copying my climactic scene in this duel!

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:19.700
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.290
Now!

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.630
Storm Access!

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:48.920
That's not enough to defeat me!

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.340
I'll now play my secret weapon!

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:56.280
Appear!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.090
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.930
The summoning conditions are two Cyberse Monsters.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:17.860
I set Bitron and Linkslayer in the Link Markers!

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.030
Circuit combine!

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:29.380
Link Summon!  Appear, Link 2 Link Bumper!

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:41.050
When there's a Cyberse on my field...

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:44.290
...I can Special Summon Backup Secretary from my hand!

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.320
Appear for a third time!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.770
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:06.420
The summoning conditions are two Cyberse Monsters.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:11.840
I set Backup Secretary and Draconnet in the Link Markers!

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.720
Circuit combine!

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:22.680
Link Summon!  Appear, Link 2 Honeybot!

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.100
And then!

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.360
What?

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.810
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.740
The summoning conditions are at least two Effect Monsters!

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:38.740
When I use a Link Monster to Link Summon...

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:42.540
...its Link Markers count as Link Materials!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:48.620
I set Link 2 Honeybot and Link 1 Link Spider in the Link Markers!

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.760
Circuit combine!

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:04.380
Link Summon!  Appear, Link 3...

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:06.210
Decode Talker!

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:17.720
Link Summon!  Appear, Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:26.120
Whoa!  He used two Link Monsters to Link Summon a Link 3 Monster!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:32.260
I equip the Equip Spell, Cyberse Annihilation, on Decode Talker.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:42.810
Then I banish Cyberse Shatter from my graveyard to activate its effect.

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:47.310
I Special Summon a Link 2 or fewer Cyberse from my graveyard.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:49.900
Resurrect, Honeybot!

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:59.120
Three Link Monsters?

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:03.560
But they're no match for my Great Ogre's ATK!

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:07.690
Our next battle will be the final one.

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:10.380
Go, Decode Talker!

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.210
You're attacking with your lowest ATK monster?

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:17.450
Since Decode Talker is equipped with Cyberse Annihilation...

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:20.980
...its ATK become the same as its opponent's.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:23.950
Decode End!

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.860
Ogre Axe!

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:40.460
One!

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:45.360
Whoa!  They're both down!

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:53.080
No way...

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.080
Is Yusaku going for a tie?

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.930
My duel is only getting started!

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:11.140
I expect nothing less.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:16.040
Due to Honeybot's effect, Decode Talker isn't destroyed in battle.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:28.060
That's why you aimed for mutual destruction.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.050
But too bad!

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.290
Great Ogre's effect!

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:37.890
By destroying one monster that's linked to it...

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.500
...it can't be destroyed!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.520
Headbatt's effect!

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:50.070
When it's sent from the field to the graveyard...

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.800
...I can add one Gouki card to my hand.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:54.800
How's that!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.540
What a turn of events!

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.900
This is unprecedented!  They've both revived!

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.560
They seem like two totally different people.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:17.530
But their wills to never give up are similar.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:22.470
Your mutual destruction failed.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.450
I wasn't aiming for mutual destruction.

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:26.900
What?

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:29.640
Link Bumper's effect!

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:35.850
Decode Talker can attack for every Link Monster on my field.

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.820
Second attack!

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.240
Attack as often as you want!

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:45.320
Okay.  If that's what you want.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.080
Due to Cyberse Annihilation's effect...

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:52.300
...Decode Talker's ATK become the same as Great Ogre's!

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:57.000
Decode End!

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:58.740
Ogre Axe!

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:20.490
Two!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:33.140
By destroying the linked Twistcobra, Great Ogre isn't destroyed!

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:39.430
Due to Honeybot's effect, Decode Talker isn't destroyed!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.780
Next, Twistcobra's effect!

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:54.590
When it's sent from the field to the graveyard, I add a new Gouki card to my hand!

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:58.560
Link Bumper's effect allows one final attack!

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:03.420
Decode Talker attacks Great Ogre!

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:06.650
Cyberse Annihilation's effect!

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:12.980
During damage calculation, my monster's ATK become the same as his opponent's!

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:21.920
Go, Decode Talker!

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:23.520
Decode End!

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.620
Great Ogre!

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:27.760
Ogre Axe!

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:51.080
Due to Honeybot's effect, Decode Talker isn't destroyed.

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.780
Great Ogre's effect!

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:58.990
When it's destroyed in battle, I can destroy a linked card instead to-

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:01.480
Oh no!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.400
You have no monsters left.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:11.070
Therefore, Great Ogre is destroyed!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.050
Cyberse Annihilation's effect activates!

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:33.020
When your monster is destroyed in battle...

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:36.960
...you take damage equal to its ATK.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:50.940
Three!

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.100
The match is over!

00:18:53.100 --> 00:19:00.500
An unbelievable comeback in Charisma Duelist Go Onizuka vs Playmaker's match!

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:04.140
The rookie Playmaker defeated Go Onizuka!

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:10.130
He wrote a new page at the dawn of the Speed Duel generation!

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.060
I lost!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:26.050
He's happy even though he lost.

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:28.380
You're not happy even though you won.

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:29.530
Why's that?

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:34.720
Win or lose, there are some duels you want to keep doing forever.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.840
Cannot comprehend!

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:49.130
Why didn't you log out right away?

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:54.110
Well, I wanted to enjoy dueling him for a bit longer.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:20:00.080
Go Onizuka...  He was a formidable opponent.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:07.680
There will come a time when we won't be enough to fight the Knights of Hanoi.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:13.320
So if he can fight on our side...

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:18.560
The fight against the Knights of Hanoi is life-or-death.

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:22.270
I don't want to involve him in that kind of dueling.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:43.300
He could've done more if he wanted to...

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:51.440
I totally lost.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:56.760
I don't know how I can face them...

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:06.900
Champion!

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:10.480
Champion, you were really cool today!

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:15.420
Go Onizuka, you'll always be our hero!

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:17.800
You guys...

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:24.580
You still think of me as a champion?

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:31.540
Even though I lost the duel?

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:34.740
Of course!

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:38.540
So you have to keep being our champion!

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:42.010
Thank you!

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:27.380
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:30.920
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:34.520
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:38.560
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:42.480
Try It over and over

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:50.640
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:57.580
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.140
Nothing is certain

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:01.820
In these isolated times

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:03.550
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.810 --> 00:23:05.320
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:08.750
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.320
The traces we leave behind

00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:16.290
The miracles we create

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:18.500
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:22.340
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.230
Two siblings only have each other.

00:23:39.440 --> 00:23:42.740
The brother's kindness proves fruitless.

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:49.210
The younger sister puts on a facade, hiding her sadness in the chaos of LINK VRAINS.

00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:52.210
In pursuit of her brother's warmth.

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:56.580
Aoi Zaizen is Blue Angel.

00:23:57.220 --> 00:24:01.860
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Idol!!  Blue Angel

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:04.560
Into the VRAINS!
